I've seen at least a couple of examples of this in the game,
particularly the quest leader - "click to continue" style lengthy
speeches.  I've been reading some of the various docs about creating
new monsters etc., but nowhere have I seen anything that specifically
discusses lengthy triggered speeches.  My guess is thus that it's a
couple of isolated instances pertaining to special encounters in the
code and not anything that would be associated with the standard
monster array(s)?

Essentially I'm looking for ways to communicate with the player at
specific intervals and with non-randomized strings.  It appears that
dialogue like the Oracle's (for example) would not be that difficult to
replicate, but that dialogue is neither ordered nor long.

Ideally I would like to find a way to either have a book-type of
delivery, which would be simpler from the triggering & logic
standpoints but I'm not sure that it would be simpler from the actual
object-creation standpoint since I haven't really seen anything like a
multipage, storable, readable text item in the game, or a speaking
character that would be capable of delivering the text on user command.
The latter would be trickier from the navigation standpoint (how to
page back and forth? does one allow that at all? are there failure
(start-over) points? etc...) but a lot of those issues are not too hard
to solve if one is willing to place the lion's share of the burden on
the user, and it's not like that'd be new to NH players :)  I could
probably engrave into a [custom] level's floor but that seems like a
terrifically arduous way to convey long text.

While I probably wouldn't be able to manage to code such a beastie
myself, I could probably find someone who could (such as easily-bribed
c-writing live-in boyfriend :), but I'd like to know where in the realm
of possibility it falls.  Anyone have any ideas?

